INT. ABANDONED PLANETARIUM GIFT SHOP - NIGHT

The shelves are half empty: plastic telescopes, glow-in-the-dark star charts, a bin of rubber moons. A velvet curtain hangs open onto the dark dome beyond. Moonlight pours through a skylight and lays a pale blue rectangle on the tile.

Five teenagers have broken in and are pretending not to be nervous.

ODELIA PEMBERTON-ROSS, seventeen, braids bound in a red scarf, sits on the checkout counter swinging her legs. ISAIAH TUPOU, eighteen, a rugby player's shoulders and a poet's quiet, stands by the curtain staring into the dark. WILHELMINA "MINA" CARVALHO, sixteen, tiny, fierce, rifles through a drawer of keychains. COLM DRISCOLL, seventeen, plugs a portable speaker into an outlet that has no power. And NERISSA "NERI" HALLORAN, seventeen, the host, sits cross-legged on the floor with a candle.

ODELIA
It's so quiet.

ISAIAH
It's a planetarium.

MINA
It's a tomb.

COLM
It's a gift shop.

NERI
It's mine for the night. Dad's the caretaker.

ODELIA
Neri, you said he was at his sister's.

NERI
He is.

COLM
(quietly)
Then who's making that noise?

They listen. A slow metallic hum, from inside the dome. They look at the curtain.

ISAIAH
It's the cooling system.

MINA
There's no power.

ISAIAH
Backup, then.

NERI
(too brightly)
Backup. Obviously.

Isaiah pulls the curtain wider. Inside, the dome's seats climb in dark rings, and at its center the old projector gleams, slowly turning on its pedestal, though nothing has turned it on.

Beside it, in a work jacket and a flashlight beam, a MAN stands motionless, watching them: GREGORY HALLORAN, fifties, Neri's father, caretaker.

GREGORY
Hello, Nerissa.

NERI
(small)
Dad.

GREGORY
Your aunt called. She says you told her I was there.

NERI
I didn't --

GREGORY
Hello, everybody. I'm Mr. Halloran. Would you like to see the stars properly?

Nobody moves. Odelia slides off the counter. Colm unplugs the speaker. Mina shuts the drawer, slowly.

The projector hums higher. The dome goes dark, and then, all at once, it fills with light: ten thousand stars wheeling in a perfect, impossible sky.

ISAIAH
(whispering)
Oh.

GREGORY
Sit. Sit. You've got till dawn.
